#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129152 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d61f93a-1acd-584c-a901-458b3cb1921e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of the Square Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6b031a4c-79e9-51a7-92a9-8bfde77cca3d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5868" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x) =\\sqrt{x}$?\n\n1. $f(x)$ is always positive.\n2. The range of $f(x)$ is $(-\\infty,0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n3. $f(x) \\rightarrow \\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow \\infty$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by recalling the graph of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt x\n$$\n\n![](images/f8/f8825f71f4d3565b28198b3a4de5424693adfead87a509f38ffecfbccb9fcd01.png)\n\nNow, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false since $f(0)=0 \\not\\gt 0$.\n- Statement II is false since the range of $f(x)$ is $[0,\\infty)$.\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $f(x) \\rightarrow \\infty$ as $x \\rightarrow \\infty$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "359b7012-75e5-5ffc-8722-9292d3f8241a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Graph of the Square Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1d895d45-a722-57fd-b429-616cf944a9c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5869" :question/problem "Which of the following could be the graph of $y = \\sqrt{x}$?\n\n![](images/76/7646aec895e67700f9ddaaa52dabb4d01edb12165add5fbc1a5b464df1a26e52.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall some of the basic properties of\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt x{:}\n$$\n\n- The point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph.\n- Its domain is $x\\in [0,\\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y\\in [0,\\infty)$.\n- The function is increasing over its entire domain.\n- As $x \\rightarrow \\infty$, we have $y\\rightarrow \\infty$, though the function increases more slowly as $x$ gets large.\n\nOf the given options, only graph II has all of the above properties.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is only II."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129152 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d61f93a-1acd-584c-a901-458b3cb1921e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of the Square Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9c0ccb8-a278-5328-b645-62a7a48db0aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127964} {:answer/id #uuid "10071b0c-c795-5fa0-9e7b-993b2f409d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127965} {:answer/id #uuid "1ed336eb-ccb3-52b9-932b-90fcd546d0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127966} {:answer/id #uuid "3a2cf1e6-30cb-5eba-96f8-e11d18a981a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127967} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1df19b-a443-5566-9480-6184a9898630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127968}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d6c25b-5295-596d-8a00-48978721711b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127963}] :question/id #uuid "ed8fdb90-e5e8-5fdc-b4ca-aa9bb4f0a24a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39552" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f(x) = \\sqrt{x}$?\n\n1. The point $(1, 2)$ lies on the graph of $y = f(x)$\n2. The domain of $f(x)$ is $x ∈ [0, ∞)$\n3. The graph of $f(x)$ lies in the second quadrant"}]}
